WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.818
Many buffer defects are only visible under specific sizes, encodings, input order, or error paths.

2
00:00:05.818 --> 00:00:13.962
A normal-path test with comfortable values may miss the boundary where capacity, length, and output size no longer line up.

3
00:00:13.962 --> 00:00:17.065
Prevention requires tests that deliberately exercise those edges.

4
00:00:17.065 --> 00:00:19.780
Sanitizers are useful development and CI tools.

5
00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:22.883
AddressSanitizer can expose invalid memory access during tests.

6
00:00:22.883 --> 00:00:27.537
UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer can reveal language-rule violations that affect size and pointer reasoning.

7
00:00:27.537 --> 00:00:32.191
Other runtime checks may help depending on compiler, platform, and build profile.

8
00:00:32.191 --> 00:00:39.948
Edge-size tests should include empty input, one element, exact capacity, one past capacity, maximum supported size, truncated input, invalid

9
00:00:39.948 --> 00:00:42.662
encoding, and output that does not fit.

10
00:00:42.662 --> 00:00:50.031
These tests should verify not only that the code rejects bad input, but also that it preserves safe state.

11
00:00:50.031 --> 00:00:55.073
Defensive fuzzing can exercise parsers and input handlers by exploring unusual input combinations.

12
00:00:55.073 --> 00:01:02.830
Keep the workflow prevention-focused: find failures, reduce them to useful regression cases, fix the underlying assumption, and add coverage.

13
00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:06.321
The goal is robust handling, not demonstration of harm.

14
00:01:06.321 --> 00:01:12.138
Findings should become tracked engineering defects with owners, fixes, regression tests, and follow-up review.

15
00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:18.732
A sanitizer report or fuzz finding is not noise just because it appears in a test build.

16
00:01:18.732 --> 00:01:22.222
It is evidence that an assumption should be corrected.

17
00:01:22.222 --> 00:01:23.773
Coverage quality determines confidence.

18
00:01:23.773 --> 00:01:26.876
Sanitizers and fuzzing only observe code that runs.

19
00:01:26.876 --> 00:01:34.245
Meaningful test harnesses inside the existing project, representative inputs, and CI integration make the results repeatable and useful without

20
00:01:34.245 --> 00:01:36.960
turning testing into a one-time event.
